sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant GW as Gateway API<br/>Kuadrant/Authorino
    participant API as API Server<br/>8080/TCP HTTP/HTTPS
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP pgx
    participant RD as Redis / Valkey<br/>6379/TCP RESP
    participant S3 as S3 Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Proc as Batch Processor<br/>9090/TCP
    participant LLM as llm-d Router<br/>HTTP/HTTPS
    participant GC as Garbage Collector<br/>9091/TCP

    Note over Client,GC: Flow 1: Batch Job Submission
    Client->>GW: POST /v1/files (multipart upload)<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    GW->>GW: Validate auth (Kuadrant/Authorino)
    GW->>API: Forward request<br/>X-MaaS-Username: tenant-id
    API->>S3: Upload input file<br/>TLS, AWS IAM/credentials
    S3-->>API: Upload confirmed
    API->>PG: Store file metadata (tenant-scoped)<br/>Optional TLS
    PG-->>API: File ID
    API-->>Client: File object (OpenAI format)

    Client->>GW: POST /v1/batches<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    GW->>API: Forward request<br/>X-MaaS-Username: tenant-id
    API->>PG: Create batch record (tenant-scoped)<br/>Optional TLS
    PG-->>API: Batch ID
    API->>RD: Enqueue to priority queue (sorted set)<br/>Optional TLS/mTLS
    RD-->>API: Enqueued
    API-->>Client: Batch object (status: validating)

    Note over Client,GC: Flow 2: Batch Job Processing
    Proc->>RD: BLMPop from priority queue<br/>Optional TLS/mTLS
    RD-->>Proc: Job dequeued
    Proc->>PG: Read batch metadata<br/>Optional TLS
    PG-->>Proc: Batch details
    Proc->>S3: Download input file<br/>TLS, AWS IAM/credentials
    S3-->>Proc: JSONL file content
    Proc->>Proc: Build per-model execution plans

    loop For each inference request (AIMD concurrency control)
        Proc->>LLM: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>Optional TLS 1.2+/mTLS<br/>Auth: API key
        LLM-->>Proc: Inference result
        alt HTTP 429 or 5xx
            Proc->>Proc: AIMD multiplicative decrease (×0.5)
        else Success
            Proc->>Proc: AIMD additive increase (+1)
        end
    end

    Proc->>S3: Upload output file<br/>TLS, AWS IAM/credentials
    S3-->>Proc: Upload confirmed
    Proc->>PG: Update batch status → completed<br/>Optional TLS
    Proc->>RD: Publish status update<br/>Optional TLS/mTLS

    Note over Client,GC: Flow 3: Batch Job Cancellation
    Client->>GW: POST /v1/batches/{id}/cancel<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    GW->>API: Forward request<br/>X-MaaS-Username: tenant-id
    API->>RD: Remove from queue (if pending)<br/>Optional TLS/mTLS
    API->>PG: Update status → cancelling<br/>Optional TLS
    API->>RD: Publish cancel event<br/>Optional TLS/mTLS
    API-->>Client: Batch object (status: cancelling)
    Proc->>RD: Receive cancel event (BLMPop)<br/>Optional TLS/mTLS
    Proc->>Proc: Drain in-flight, skip remaining
    Proc->>PG: Update status → cancelled<br/>Optional TLS

    Note over Client,GC: Flow 4: Garbage Collection
    loop Every 1h (configurable)
        GC->>PG: Query expired batches/files<br/>Optional TLS
        PG-->>GC: Expired records
        GC->>S3: Delete expired files<br/>TLS, AWS IAM/credentials
        GC->>PG: Delete expired metadata<br/>Optional TLS
    end

    loop Every 60m (reconciler)
        GC->>RD: Check in-flight heartbeats<br/>Optional TLS/mTLS
        RD-->>GC: Stale entries (crashed processors)
        GC->>PG: Re-enqueue or fail orphaned jobs<br/>Optional TLS
        GC->>RD: Update queue state<br/>Optional TLS/mTLS
    end
